<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  launchd agent for the Claude Code OAuth token-refresher (ce-cs3v).

  Keeps ~/.claude/.credentials.json fresh so the VROOM supervisor mesh (three
  Claude Code sessions sharing one credentials file) survives access-token
  expiry without a human re-running /login. This is the IDLE BACKSTOP: it runs
  even when no session is active, so the credentials file never goes stale and
  the single-use refresh-token family never dies of neglect.

  WARNING -- the single-writer invariant this job was designed around is VOID.
  It assumed a retired `apiKeyHelper` (not to be restored) drove on-demand
  refresh through this same binary during active sessions, so both paths shared
  one cross-process file lock and could never race or double-spend the refresh
  token. That apiKeyHelper was removed on 2026-07-10 because Claude Code
  >=2.1.205 treats it as an external API key that shadows healthy OAuth
  (anthropics/claude-code#11587). Since then this binary is the ONLY refresher
  that takes the lock, while ~15 other OAuth clients on the host (the
  Desktop-embedded claude-code runtime, CLI sessions, agm sandbox spawns) each
  refresh independently against the same credentials file. Nothing prevents one
  of them from presenting an already-spent refresh token, which the server
  treats as replay and answers by revoking the entire family. Restoring a real
  single-writer guarantee is tracked in ce-77ip; until then this job carries
  -cadence so a death is at least ALERTED and SURVIVED rather than silent.

  Runs without -force so each tick refreshes only when the access token is near
  expiry. Claude Code runtimes also refresh this shared credentials file and do
  not take dear-agent's lock, so forced 30-minute rotations widen the refresh
  replay race instead of preventing it.

  -expiry-skew MUST stay larger than StartInterval. Dropping -force alone left a
  worse bug: the default skew is 60s but this job only looks every 1800s, so a
  tick almost always finds the token "fresh" with minutes left, does nothing,
  and the NEXT tick arrives with the token already expired. Observed on
  2026-08-15: the token died at 09:21:24Z, the 08:53:43Z tick declined to
  refresh, and the 09:23:43Z tick refreshed 2m19s too late -- every request in
  that window got a 401 "login expired". A skew wider than the tick guarantees
  some tick always sees the expiry coming and rotates ahead of it.

  That margin is also what keeps the family alive. A token refreshed well before
  expiry is never near-expiry from a Claude Code runtime's point of view, so no
  other client on the host has cause to rotate it -- this job stays the de facto
  single writer without needing a lock the other clients do not take.

  stdout carries ONLY the access token
  (stdout-only token contract), so it is routed to /dev/null to keep the secret
  out of the log file; structured logs and the JSONL audit trail go to stderr /
  ~/.local/state/dear-agent.

  The plist is a TEMPLATE: the install target
  (make install-token-refresher-launchagent) substitutes __HOME__ for the real
  home directory before staging it into ~/Library/LaunchAgents.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.dear-agent.token-refresher</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>__HOME__/go/bin/token-refresher</string>
    <string>-cadence</string>
    <!-- Must exceed StartInterval below; see the header note. -->
    <string>-expiry-skew</string>
    <string>45m</string>
  </array>

  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>__HOME__/go/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin</string>
    <key>HOME</key>
    <string>__HOME__</string>
  </dict>

  <!-- Check every 30 minutes; refresh only when the access token is within
       -expiry-skew (45m) of expiring. Keep this BELOW the skew above. -->
  <key>StartInterval</key>
  <integer>1800</integer>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>

  <!-- Never let two refreshes overlap (they share the credentials lock). -->
  <key>AbandonProcessGroup</key>
  <false/>

  <!-- stdout is the access token (stdout-only token contract) — discard it so the
       secret never lands in a log file. -->
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/dev/null</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>__HOME__/.local/state/dear-agent/token-refresher.err.log</string>

  <key>ProcessType</key>
  <string>Background</string>

  <!-- Working dir: user's home. launchd otherwise starts jobs with cwd=/ (ce-k414). -->
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>__HOME__</string>
</dict>
</plist>
